<article class="env-remark" id="0F74">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F74">Remark <span data-tag="0F74">63.3.9</span> <span class="named">(Open embeddings and compactly supported sections)</span>.</a>  Let $X$ be a separated scheme locally of finite type over a field $k$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an abelian sheaf on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$. Exactly as in Remark <a href="/tag/0F53" data-tag="0F53">63.3.5</a> for $X' \subset X$ open there is an injective map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  H^0_ c(X', \mathcal{F}|_{X'}) \longrightarrow H^0_ c(X, \mathcal{F})  \]
</div>
  <p> and these maps turn $H^0_ c$ into a “cosheaf” on the Zariski site of $X$. </p>
</article>